Rem ==================================================================
Rem buzzer.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: the buzzer
Rem
Rem A West Riding mill ran on sound, and the buzzer was the one sound
Rem the mill made on purpose. This machine is the derived layer over
Rem the sound builtins (Sound, NoteOn, NoteOff, SoundQueue, SoundStop,
Rem SoundGain, SoundWave): note names, MIDI numbers, and a
Rem GW-BASIC-subset MML player — Play(1, "T120 O4 L8 C D E F G2").
Rem
Rem SoundWave(ch, w) picks a channel's timbre, sticky like SoundGain:
Rem 0 square (the default, and the only voice Sound's anonymous pool
Rem speaks), 1 triangle, 2 sine. Squares are bright and chip-like but
Rem below ~60 Hz they read as a click train — the edges are all a small
Rem speaker can voice — so deep bass wants sine or triangle. Changing
Rem the wave re-voices a held note in place at its current pitch.
Rem
Rem Sound is audible under `mill run` and `mill dap`. Woven output run
Rem via bare `dotnet`, and any machine with no audio device, is SILENT:
Rem every sound word is a no-op there, never an error — though bad
Rem arguments (channel 0, negative duration) raise even in silence.
Rem
Rem The frequency word is MidiFreq, never Freq — stats.shoddy exports
Rem Freq and both would fold to FREQ. The note record's fields are
Rem FreqHz and Ms for the same reason.
Rem
Rem MmlNotes is PURE — MML string in, note list out, no I/O — so scores
Rem parse and test headless. Play is just SoundQueue over its output:
Rem it returns as soon as the tune is queued, which is immediately.
Rem ==================================================================


Rem ---- waveforms -------------------------------------------------------
Rem Names for SoundWave's argument, so programs read as music rather
Rem than magic numbers.

Def WaveSquare() As Number
    0

Def WaveTriangle() As Number
    1

Def WaveSine() As Number
    2

Rem ---- notes and frequencies ------------------------------------------

Type BuzzerNote
    FreqHz As Number            Rem 0 = rest
    Ms As Number

Rem A4 = MIDI 69 = 440 Hz, equal temperament. Fractional MIDI numbers
Rem are legal (quarter-tones, pitch bends) — nothing here rounds.
Def MidiFreq(midi As Number) As Number
    440 * 2 ^ ((midi - 69) / 12)

Rem "C4" -> 60, "F#3" -> 54, "Bb5" -> 82. Scientific pitch: C4 is middle
Rem C. Letters A-G, "#" sharp, "b" flat, octave digit 0-8 required.
Rem THE GUARDED TWIN, and the aborting one defined over it. This is the
Rem shape TryReadFile and ReadFile have in the runtime, brought up to a
Rem machine for the first time — and it is here because a MACHINE is
Rem where this parse lives, so a guarded builtin could not have helped.
Rem
Rem Everything that can be malformed is decided in the Try form, and
Rem NoteMidi is that answer with the Err turned back into the abort it
Rem always was. So there is ONE set of rules rather than a parser and a
Rem validator that can drift apart, and a caller who would rather be
Rem told than killed has somewhere to go.
Def TryNoteMidi(name As String) As Result
    TryNoteAt(name, Upper(name))

Def TryNoteAt(name As String, u As String) As Result
    If Len(u) < 2 Or Instr("ABCDEFG", Mid(u, 1, 1)) = 0 Then
        Err(NoteWhy(name), 0)
    Else
        TryNoteOct(name, u, 2 + MmlAccLen(u, 2, "#B"))

Def TryNoteOct(name As String, u As String, ka As Number) As Result
    If Len(u) <> ka Or Instr("012345678", Mid(u, ka, 1)) = 0 Then
        Err(NoteWhy(name), 0)
    Else
        Ok(12 * (Val(Mid(u, ka, 1)) + 1) + MmlBase(Mid(u, 1, 1)) + MmlAccVal(u, 2, "#B"))

Def NoteWhy(name As String) As String
    "NOTEMIDI: BAD NOTE NAME '" & name & "'"

Def NoteMidi(name As String) As Number
    NoteMidiOr(TryNoteMidi(name))

Def NoteMidiOr(r As Result) As Number
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(m)
            m
        Case Err(w, at)
            Error(w)
        Case Else
            Error("NOTEMIDI: THE NAME DID NOT ANSWER")

Def NoteFreq(name As String) As Number
    MidiFreq(NoteMidi(name))

Rem ---- MML (Music Macro Language), GW-BASIC subset ---------------------
Rem Case-insensitive, whitespace ignored.
Rem   A-G   a note; optional # or + (sharp), - (flat); optional length
Rem         (4 = quarter, 8 = eighth...); optional trailing . (x1.5)
Rem   On    octave 0-8, default 4 (scientific: O4 contains middle C —
Rem         GW-BASIC's octaves sat one lower)
Rem   < >   octave down / up
Rem   Ln    default length, default 4
Rem   Tn    tempo in quarter notes per minute, default 120
Rem   Pn Rn a rest of length n (dotted allowed)
Rem   ,     a quarter-note rest — always length 4, whatever Ln says
Rem A whole note is 4 * 60000 / T ms; length n divides it. A malformed
Rem string raises naming the offending position. GW-BASIC's MN/ML/MS
Rem articulation modes, Nn, and per-note volume are left for later.

Rem PURE: parse MML to a note list, no I/O.
Def TryMmlNotes(mml As String) As Result
    MmlRun(Upper(mml), 1, 4, 4, 120)

Def MmlNotes(mml As String) As List Of BuzzerNote
    MmlNotesOr(TryMmlNotes(mml))

Def MmlNotesOr(r As Result) As List Of BuzzerNote
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(ns)
            ns
        Case Err(w, at)
            Error(w)
        Case Else
            Error("MML: THE PARSE DID NOT ANSWER")

Rem Queue every note of an MML string onto channel ch. Fire-and-forget.
Def Play(ch As Number, mml As String)
    PlayNotes(ch, MmlNotes(mml))

Rem The queue half of Play, for programmatically built scores.
Def PlayNotes(ch As Number, notes As List Of BuzzerNote)
    If Not IsEmpty(notes) Then
        SoundQueue(ch, FreqHz(First(notes)), Ms(First(notes)))
        PlayNotes(ch, Rest(notes))

Rem ---- the parser (internal; s is already uppercased) ------------------

Rem THE PARSE THREADS A Result, and MmlNotes is that answer with the Err
Rem turned back into the abort it always was. Every recursive step
Rem unwraps what came back and passes a failure straight out, so the
Rem five ways an MML string can be malformed each have exactly one
Rem statement of what is wrong and where — no second walk to drift.
Rem
Rem It reads longer than the aborting version did, and all of the extra
Rem is unwrapping. That is what threading a failure through a recursive
Rem descent costs in a language with no exceptions, and it buys a
Rem parser a session can be handed without the session being at risk.
Def MmlRun(s As String, k As Number, oct As Number, dlen As Number, tempo As Number) As Result
    If k > Len(s) Then
        Ok({ })
    Else
        If Mid(s, k, 1) = " " Or Mid(s, k, 1) = Chr(9) Then
            MmlRun(s, k + 1, oct, dlen, tempo)
        Else
            MmlCmd(Mid(s, k, 1), s, k, oct, dlen, tempo)

Def MmlCmd(c As String, s As String, k As Number, oct As Number, dlen As Number, tempo As Number) As Result
    Select Case c
        Case "T"
            MmlWithTempo(s, k, oct, dlen, MmlArg(s, k, "T"))
        Case "L"
            MmlWithLen(s, k, oct, tempo, MmlArg(s, k, "L"))
        Case "O"
            MmlWithOctArg(s, k, dlen, tempo, MmlArg(s, k, "O"))
        Case "<"
            MmlWithOct(s, k + 1, dlen, tempo, MmlMustOct(oct - 1, k))
        Case ">"
            MmlWithOct(s, k + 1, dlen, tempo, MmlMustOct(oct + 1, k))
        Case "P", "R"
            MmlStep(s, k, k + 1, 0, oct, dlen, tempo)
        Case ","
            MmlOnto(BuzzerNote(0, MmlMs(tempo, 4, 0)), MmlRun(s, k + 1, oct, dlen, tempo))
        Case "A", "B", "C", "D", "E", "F", "G"
            MmlStep(s, k, k + 1 + MmlAccLen(s, k + 1, "#+-"), 12 * (oct + 1) + MmlBase(c) + MmlAccVal(s, k + 1, "#+-"), oct, dlen, tempo)
        Case Else
            Err("MML: UNEXPECTED '" & c & "' AT POSITION " & Str(k), k)

Rem The four commands that carry a number: each takes the argument's
Rem Result, and either goes on with it or hands the failure straight
Rem out. Written apart rather than as one because each puts its number
Rem in a different place.
Def MmlWithTempo(s As String, k As Number, oct As Number, dlen As Number, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(t)
            MmlRun(s, MmlDigitEnd(s, k + 1), oct, dlen, t)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            MmlBroke()

Def MmlWithLen(s As String, k As Number, oct As Number, tempo As Number, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(n)
            MmlRun(s, MmlDigitEnd(s, k + 1), oct, n, tempo)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            MmlBroke()

Rem O takes its argument AND then has to be in range, so it unwraps
Rem twice — the argument first, the octave it implies second.
Def MmlWithOctArg(s As String, k As Number, dlen As Number, tempo As Number, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(o)
            MmlWithOct(s, MmlDigitEnd(s, k + 1), dlen, tempo, MmlMustOct(o - 1, k))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            MmlBroke()

Def MmlWithOct(s As String, k As Number, dlen As Number, tempo As Number, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(o)
            MmlRun(s, k, o, dlen, tempo)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            MmlBroke()

Rem One note (midi > 0) or rest (midi 0) starting at k, its optional
Rem length digits starting at kl: read length and dot, emit, carry on.
Def MmlStep(s As String, k As Number, kl As Number, midi As Number, oct As Number, dlen As Number, tempo As Number) As Result
    MmlStepLen(s, k, MmlDigitEnd(s, kl), midi, oct, dlen, tempo, MmlLenAt(s, kl, MmlDigitEnd(s, kl), dlen, k))

Def MmlStepLen(s As String, k As Number, ke As Number, midi As Number, oct As Number, dlen As Number, tempo As Number, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(n)
            MmlOnto(BuzzerNote(MmlPitch(midi), MmlMs(tempo, n, MmlDots(s, ke))),
                    MmlRun(s, ke + MmlDots(s, ke), oct, dlen, tempo))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            MmlBroke()

Rem A note in front of whatever the rest of the string came to — or that
Rem failure, unchanged. This is where the list is actually built, and the
Rem only place it is.
Def MmlOnto(n As BuzzerNote, rest As Result) As Result
    Select Case rest
        Case Ok(ns)
            Ok(Prepend(n, ns))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            MmlBroke()

Rem The Case Else every unwrap above needs and none of them can reach: a
Rem Result is Ok or Err and there is no third. Stated once rather than
Rem eight times, so the eight read as the two cases they are.
Def MmlBroke() As Result
    Err("MML: THE PARSE DID NOT ANSWER", 0)

Def MmlPitch(midi As Number) As Number
    If midi = 0 Then
        0
    Else
        MidiFreq(midi)

Def MmlMs(tempo As Number, n As Number, dots As Number) As Number
    (4 * 60000 / tempo) / n * (1 + dots * 0.5)

Def MmlLenAt(s As String, kl As Number, ke As Number, dlen As Number, k As Number) As Result
    If ke = kl Then
        Ok(dlen)
    Else
        If Val(Mid(s, kl, ke - kl)) < 1 Then
            Err("MML: BAD LENGTH AT POSITION " & Str(k), k)
        Else
            Ok(Val(Mid(s, kl, ke - kl)))

Rem A command's required numeric argument (T, L, O), validated >= 1 —
Rem O is passed shifted by one so O0 survives the check.
Def MmlArg(s As String, k As Number, what As String) As Result
    MmlArgAt(s, k, what, MmlDigitEnd(s, k + 1))

Def MmlArgAt(s As String, k As Number, what As String, e As Number) As Result
    If e = k + 1 Then
        Err("MML: " & what & " NEEDS A NUMBER AT POSITION " & Str(k), k)
    Else
        MmlArgVal(s, k, what, Val(Mid(s, k + 1, e - k - 1)))

Def MmlArgVal(s As String, k As Number, what As String, v As Number) As Result
    If what = "O" Then
        Ok(v + 1)
    Else
        If v < 1 Then
            Err("MML: " & what & " MUST BE AT LEAST 1 AT POSITION " & Str(k), k)
        Else
            Ok(v)

Def MmlMustOct(oct As Number, k As Number) As Result
    If oct < 0 Or oct > 8 Then
        Err("MML: OCTAVE OUT OF RANGE 0-8 AT POSITION " & Str(k), k)
    Else
        Ok(oct)

Def MmlBase(c As String) As Number
    Select Case c
        Case "C"
            0
        Case "D"
            2
        Case "E"
            4
        Case "F"
            5
        Case "G"
            7
        Case "A"
            9
        Case Else
            11

Rem accs is the accidental set: "#+-" in MML (where B is a note), "#B"
Rem in note names (where b uppercases to B and - never appears).
Def MmlAccLen(s As String, k As Number, accs As String) As Number
    If k <= Len(s) And Instr(accs, Mid(s, k, 1)) > 0 Then
        1
    Else
        0

Def MmlAccVal(s As String, k As Number, accs As String) As Number
    If MmlAccLen(s, k, accs) = 0 Then
        0
    Else
        If Instr("#+", Mid(s, k, 1)) > 0 Then
            1
        Else
            -1

Def MmlDots(s As String, k As Number) As Number
    If k <= Len(s) And Mid(s, k, 1) = "." Then
        1
    Else
        0

Def MmlDigitEnd(s As String, k As Number) As Number
    If k > Len(s) Then
        k
    Else
        If Instr("0123456789", Mid(s, k, 1)) > 0 Then
            MmlDigitEnd(s, k + 1)
        Else
            k
